# {{appName}}

Go client for {{appName}} {{version}}, generated by openapi-generator
(go-fetch). It imports only the standard library and needs Go 1.24.

```go
cfg := &{{packageName}}.Configuration{
	HTTPClient: &http.Client{Timeout: 10 * time.Second},
}
```

Every operation has three methods on the API type of its tag:

| Method       | Returns                                           |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `Xxx`        | the decoded body                                  |
| `XxxRaw`     | the `*http.Response` of a 2xx status, body unread |
| `XxxRequest` | the `*http.Request`, not sent                     |

A status outside 2xx is a `*{{packageName}}.ResponseError`; its `Model` holds
the body decoded into the type the spec gives for that status.
